# Agent workflow (skills)

Skills under `.cursor/skills/` are **opt-in** (`disable-model-invocation: true`). **Do not** load or follow a skill until the user names it or the trigger phrase below applies.

| Skill | Load only when |
|-------|----------------|
| `feature-kickoff` | User says **kickoff**, **plan the feature**, **before we code**, or asks for issue scope/acceptance criteria |
| `feature-ship` | User says **ship**, **ship it**, **ready for review**, **open PR**, **merge**, or **definition of done** |
| `tray-ui-change` | User says **tray-ui-change** or asks for UI handoff after WPF/XAML edits |
| `security-pass` | User says **security pass** or asks for a security review |
| `performance-pass` | User says **performance pass** or asks about orchestrator/log slowness |

**Do not** auto-run kickoff on every bug/feature mention. **Do not** auto-run security-pass + performance-pass before every PR.

**Order (when user drives full flow):** kickoff → implement → ship. Security/performance only if warranted or user asks.

**Schema / tests / build:** `testing.mdc`, `no-unapproved-runtime-execution.mdc` — not skill files.

**Issues before commit (moderate):** see `work-tracking.mdc` — link GitHub Issue for features/bugs; chores can opt out.
